rigger.js and index.html are pinned test oracles copied from the upstream source.
Production uses a byte-for-byte parity-tested TypeScript rigger port in
../upstream/rigger.ts; the runtime port remains isolated until its frame parity
suite is complete.
The generic close-diff RGBA data and decoder are ported in
../upstream/genericParts.ts; tests pin the decoded pixels by SHA-256.
The UMD boot line in rigger.js is adjusted so the oracle loads under ESM; the
rigger algorithm itself is unchanged. index.html is byte-for-byte unmodified.
The base bind, deform, and fade math follows index.html. Myriad supplies its own
bounded ambient and text-free preview speech timing.
The surrounding Myriad page, overlay, and settings chrome are not from that project.
